From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: rpcd: exec: observe EOF before invalidating pipe fds

Commit 26dba5206e17 moved the stdout and stderr descriptor
invalidation before the final ustream polls. Once the descriptor is set
to -1, ustream_poll() cannot observe EOF and the exec plugin request
remains deferred until its timeout despite the child having exited.

Poll both streams after closing their descriptors, then invalidate the
stored descriptor numbers. The deferred reply cannot run until the
callback returns, so this preserves the double-close protection while
allowing the stream state callbacks to complete the request.

Fixes: 26dba5206e17 ("exec: prevent double close() of exec pipe descriptors")
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/exec.c
+++ b/exec.c
@@ -196,14 +196,14 @@
 	close(c->opipe.fd.fd);
 	close(c->epipe.fd.fd);
 
+	ustream_poll(&c->opipe.stream);
+	ustream_poll(&c->epipe.stream);
+
 	/* ustream_free() does not reset the fd, and rpc_exec_reply() closes it
 	 * again later.  Mark the descriptors as consumed so that the second
 	 * close() cannot accidentally close an unrelated, meanwhile reused fd. */
 	c->opipe.fd.fd = -1;
 	c->epipe.fd.fd = -1;
-
-	ustream_poll(&c->opipe.stream);
-	ustream_poll(&c->epipe.stream);
 }
 
 static void
